# Week 5 – Budget Management

## Overview
This project demonstrates a budget management application developed using Python. It focuses on managing budget-related operations and testing the functionality using automated tests.

## Objectives
- Understand budget management logic using Python.
- Implement budget-related functionality.
- Organize Python code into modules.
- Validate functionality using unit testing.

## Technologies Used
- Python
- Pytest
- VS Code

## Project Structure

```text
Week-5/
├── budget.py
├── test_budget.py
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md
```

## Installation

1. Clone the repository:

   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/laxmispandana-wq/GEN-AI_2520030160.git
   ```

2. Navigate to the Week-5 folder:

   ```bash
   cd GEN-AI_2520030160/LAB/Week-5
   ```

3. Install dependencies:

   ```bash
   pip install -r requirements.txt
   ```

## Execution

Run the project:

```bash
python budget.py
```

## Testing

Run the test file:

```bash
python -m pytest test_budget.py
```

## Working

The project implements budget-related operations through Python functions and validates their behavior using automated testing. The test file checks the functionality of the budget logic to help identify errors and ensure expected behavior.

## Learning Outcomes
- Writing modular Python programs.
- Understanding budget-related logic.
- Writing and executing unit tests.
- Validating code using automated testing.

